          "title": "You'll want to know: चिकित्सति",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चिकित्सति — cikitsati — \"treats a patient\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "वैद्यः रुग्णं बालं चिकित्सति। vaidyaḥ rugṇaṃ bālaṃ cikitsati. The physician treats the sick child."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he …): सः रुग्णं बालं चिकित्सितवान्, saḥ rugṇaṃ bālaṃ cikitsitavān."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चिकित्सति (cikitsati) is built on the desiderative of the root √cit, \"to perceive, to care for\", the word behind चिकित्सकः; MW gives \"to treat medically, cure\" (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
